      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T00:33:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Phone process crash and modem crash cases are planned to handle after IC.\n\nBut one important case is that, when modem reboot, DSM will set default system thresholds define here during onReset(). So if the onReset() occur when device is idle,  even no app has set isSystemThresholdReportingRequestedWhileIdle, we have to honor the default system thresholds set here.\n\nThat\u0027s why this flag is introduced and the isRadioResetOngoing() is checked in SST#shouldHonorSystemThresholds.\n\nThis flag should be able to replaced with better solution after IC when we formally support Phone or Modem crash cases.",
      "parentUuid": "db9801b8_80a39b79",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "6f1ff79e7f067f2a3fc0b3b46bec673ee46ca14f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
